    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1177">

                <pb facs="0967" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.633/5–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-21T10:00:00+08:00">May 21, 1949—10 a.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 21—2:13 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>876. ReDeptel 299, May 17. Letter dated May 19 southeast [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >sent</hi>] headquarters PLA, double registry, yesterday in sense directed.
                    Letter <pb facs="0968" n="958" xml:id="pg958"/> same date mailed Ward express
                    double registry today, enclosing copies 2 letters headquarters and
                    Depreftel.</p>
                <p>Letters to headquarters requested travel facilities for Manhard [and]
                    Armstrong.</p>
                <p>ReDeptel 278, May 13,<anchor n="56" xml:id="d1177-f1"/> perforce of course
                    addressed headquarters PLA as such. Since proposed in event nonreply however
                    address either Chu Teh<anchor n="57" xml:id="d1177-f2"/> or Mao Tse-tung or both
                    re subject, re Contel 860 [<hi rendition="#italic">896</hi>] May 18,<anchor
                        n="58" xml:id="d1177-f3"/> please instruct re mode address in present
                    instance.</p>
                <p>Copy letter to Ward and enclosure sent Tientsin for information.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 876, repeated Nanking 569, OffEmb Canton 129, Shanghai 588.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1177-f1" n="56" xml:id="d1177-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram No. 98 to the Consul General at Tientsin, <ref target="#pg1082"
                        >p. 1082</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1177-f2" n="57" xml:id="d1177-f2-content">
                <p>Commander in Chief of Chinese Communist armies.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1177-f3" n="58" xml:id="d1177-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Post</hi>, <ref target="#pg1084">p. 1084</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
